We apply the following patches to the upstream source code, both in
libtommath/bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c:

1) Guard the platform-specific calls in s_mp_rand_platform() with the
   preprocessor.

   Upstream guards these calls with MP_HAS() and relies on the compiler to
   eliminate the calls to the functions that are not defined for the target
   platform. Clang does not do this without optimization, which makes
   linking fail (upstream's CMake build works around this by forcing -O1).

2) Fill the entire buffer in s_read_urandom() when read() returns less than
   requested.

   The read loop always reads into the beginning of the buffer, leaving the
   rest of it without random data. This is a backport of upstream commit
   528fdb0 (s_mp_rand_platform.c: s_read_urandom: correctly handle split
   read), which is not yet in a release.

The patches were made as follows:

$ cd libtommath/
$ mv bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.orig
$ cp -H bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.orig bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c
$ edit bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c
$ diff -u bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.orig bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c \
  >bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.patch

To re-apply them after upgrading the upstream submodule:

$ cd libtommath/
$ cp -H bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.orig bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c
$ patch <bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.patch

Upstream renamed this file to s_mp_rand_platform.c on its develop branch,
where patch 2 is already applied and patch 1 is still required.
